  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Co-Creating Green Safe Spaces</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project strengthens and scales up the Co-Creating Green Safe Spaces (CGSS) initiative in Zimbabwe, empowering youth in Domboshava to become leaders and advocates for sustainability, inclusion, and climate resilience. Building on the 2024 pilot, it will establish an additional youth-led hub and expand youth participation. Through non-formal education and experiential learning, youth will practice agroecology, water conservation, floriculture, agroforestry, and apiculture, while fostering dialogue on inclusion and participation. Two intellectual outputs will be developed: a Toolbox on Life Skills for climate-smart practices and inclusion, and a Guidebook on Green Safe Spaces providing a replicable model for youth-led sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
